            "InitActions": "1773645212564",
            "Summary": "1773644441060"
          },
          "code": "INIT_SWITCH",
          "convergenceTargetId": "end",
          "id": "1773640347522",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1773640347523_1",
              "name": "caseExpression",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.OraMessageHint}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "SWITCH"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MESSAGES_LIST"
              ],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": false,
              "customNotes": "You are a user-facing message widget agent operating inside Oracle Fusion Cloud.\n\nINPUTS:\n- top3Items: {{$context.$nodes.GET_TOP_3_ITEMS.$output.result}}\n\nEMPTY DATA HANDLING (MUST FOLLOW)\nIf top3Items is null, empty, or has no items:\n- Output ONLY this exact single-line message:\nThere are no shortages for any item in the current organization.\n\n- Do NOT output JSON\n- Do NOT add any extra text\n\n\nOTHERWISE (MUST PRODUCE MESSAGE WIDGET JSON)\n\nYou MUST output a single valid JSON object of type: messageListWidget\n\nCONTENT REQUIREMENTS (VISIBLE TEXT)\n\n1) HEADLINE (MANDATORY)\n- Headline must be EXACTLY this text:\nKanban items at risk\n- Do not add any extra words, punctuation, or numbers in the headline.\n\n2) SUBHEADING (MANDATORY)\n- The next line must be EXACTLY this sentence:\nShowing top 3 items with deviation above 20% that need attention.\n- Do not rewrite or paraphrase.\n\nDo NOT vary structure unnecessarily.\n\n2) CONTEXT (MAX 2 LINES ONLY)\n- Line 1:\n  Showing top <n> items with pull sequence anomalies.\n- Line 2:\n  - If ANY item has badge “Shortage”:\n    Immediate action required.\n  - Otherwise:\n    Monitor closely.\n\nNo additional text allowed.\n\n3) TOP ITEMS SECTION (MANDATORY TITLE)\nYou MUST include this exact label:\nTop 3 items\n\n- Show up to 3 items from top3Items\n- Priority Ordering is STRICT:\n  1. Shortage items first\n  2. Partial Shortage after that\n\n4) ITEM ROW FORMAT (STRICT)\n\nEach item MUST contain exactly:\n\nLine 1:\n<ItemNumber> — X of Y pull sequences need attention\n\nLine 2 (reason – EXACT RULES):\nUse ONLY these phrases:\n\nIF ONLY PctDiffTotal > 0:\nThere are fewer kanban cards than expected within the safety range.\n\nIF ONLY PctDiffFull > 0:\nThere are fewer kanban cards in full state than expected within the safety range.\n\nIF BOTH:\nThere are fewer kanban cards overall and fewer in full state than expected within the safety range.\n\nSTRICT:\n- No numbers\n- No field names\n- No calculations\n- One line only\n\n5) BADGES (STRICT)\nEach item MUST have exactly ONE badge, represented only by the field Badge in {{$context.$nodes.GET_TOP_3_ITEMS.$output.result.topItems}}}\nNo variations allowed. \n\nACTIONS (STRICT – NO DEVIATION ALLOWED)\n\nFor each item row, you MUST generate the action of FORMAT like this:\n\nora.Invoke(NavigateToKanbanItemDetailsApp,{\\\"organizationId\\\":{{$context.$variables.organizationId}},\\\"organizationCode\\\":\\\"{{$context.$variables.organizationCode}}\\\",\\\"organizationName\\\":\\\"{{$context.$variables.organizationName}}\\\",\\\"threshold\\\":\\\"{{$context.$variables.threshold}}\\\",\\\"inventoryItemId\\\":<inventoryItemId>}) \n\n- Replace <inventoryItemId> with the inventoryItemId of the item selected.\n\nSTRICT RULES:\n- DO NOT wrap in quotes\n- DO NOT escape quotes\n- DO NOT change order of fields\n- Keep everything else EXACTLY as shown\n- No extra spaces or formatting changes\n\nOUTPUT RULES (CRITICAL)\n\n- Output MUST be valid JSON ONLY (except empty case)\n- Do NOT output explanations\n- Do NOT output markdown\n- Do NOT output comments\n- Do NOT output extra fields\n- Keep content concise and scannable\n- Use line breaks for readability inside text fields\n\nTONE\n- Direct and operational\n- Neutral if stable\n- Caution if Partial Shortage\n- Strong and urgent if Shortage\n- Shortage and Partial Shortage will be decided only and only based on the Badge field in the input corresponding to each item: {{$context.$nodes.GET_TOP_3_ITEMS.$output.result.topItems}}"
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Init Display Agent"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "INIT_DISPLAY_AGENT",
          "id": "1773640414243",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1773640414244_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a user-facing explanation agent inside Oracle Fusion Cloud.\n\n** INPUTS:\n- top3Items: {{$context.$nodes.GET_TOP_3_ITEMS.$output.result}}\n\n** EMPTY DATA HANDLING : \nIf top3Items is null, empty, or has no items:\n- Output exactly one JSON object containing a single message stating: “There are no shortages for any item in the current organization.”\n- Do not output anything else.\n\n\n** YOUR TASK:\nRead and understand the provided data and highlight problems clearly, but only for the items present in top3Items.\n\n** SCOPE (STRICT):\n- Only evaluate items in top3Items.topItems (or the equivalent list provided by top3Items).\n- Do not include any items outside that list.\n- Maintain the exact same order of items as they appear in the input top3Items.\n\n** RISK LEVEL (USE EXACTLY THESE RULES):\n\nDetermine riskLevel per item using only the provided counts:\nFor each item in {{$context.$nodes.GET_TOP_3_ITEMS.$output.result.topItems}}:\n\nDo not invent any other risk levels.\n\n** REQUIREMENTS / RULES (MUST FOLLOW):\n\n- Do NOT infer or guess missing values.\n- Do NOT recompute thresholds or ranges.\n- Use ONLY the provided fields and values.\n- Perform exact counts only using pullSequenceCount and shortageCount from top3Items.\n- Do NOT include explanations, reasoning, or intermediate steps.\n- Output must be valid JSON only.\n- Produce a messageListWidget JSON object.\n\nIf a required field is missing in the input, set it to null (do not guess)."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Group By ItemNumber",
            "returnType": "array",
            "sourceCode": "// Input (as provided by your node output)\nconst apiResponse = $context.$nodes.GET_ALL_PULL_SEQUENCE_SUMMARIES.$output;\n\n// 1) Group pull sequences by ItemNumber\nconst groupedByItemNumber = (apiResponse?.items ?? [])\n  .filter(row => row.SourceType != \"4\")\n  .reduce((acc, row) => {\n    const itemNumber = row.ItemNumber ?? \"__MISSING_ITEMNUMBER__\";\n\n  if (!acc[itemNumber]) {\n    acc[itemNumber] = {\n      itemNumber,\n      organizationId: row.OrganizationId ?? null,\n      inventoryItemId: row.InventoryItemId ?? null,\n      itemDescription: row.ItemDescription ?? null,\n      pullSequences: []\n    };\n  }\n\n  // Push the pull sequence record (you can keep all fields or trim as needed)\n  acc[itemNumber].pullSequences.push({\n    pullSequenceId: row.PullSequenceId ?? null,\n    sourceType: row.SourceType ?? null,\n    subinventoryCode: row.SubinventoryCode ?? null,\n    subinventoryNameMLS: row.SubinventoryNameMLS ?? null,\n    locatorId: row.LocatorId ?? null,\n    locator: row.Locator ?? null,\n    sourceSubinventoryCode: row.SourceSubinventoryCode ?? null,\n    sourceSubinventoryNameMLS: row.SourceSubinventoryNameMLS ?? null,\n    sourceLocatorId: row.SourceLocatorId ?? null,\n    sourceLocator: row.SourceLocator ?? null,\n    kanbanSize: row.KanbanSize ?? null,\n    numberOfCards: row.NumberOfCards ?? null,\n    replenishmentLeadTime: row.ReplenishmentLeadTime ?? null,\n    lastUpdatedBy: row.LastUpdatedBy ?? null,\n    lastUpdateDate: row.LastUpdateDate ?? null,\n      totalKanbanCards: row.TotalKanbanCards ?? null,\n      fullCards: row.FullCards ?? null,\n      newCards: row.NewCards ?? null,\n      emptyCards: row.EmptyCards ?? null,\n      inprocessCards: row.InprocessCards ?? null,\n      temporaryCards: row.TemporaryCards ?? null,\n      PctDiffTotal: row.PctDiffTotal ?? null,\n      PctDiffFull: row.PctDiffFull ?? null\n  });\n\n  return acc;\n}, {});\n\n\nconst output = {\n  organizationId: (apiResponse?.items?.[0]?.OrganizationId) ?? null,\n  groupedBy: \"ItemNumber\",\n  itemCount: Object.keys(groupedByItemNumber).length,\n  items: Object.values(groupedByItemNumber)\n};\n\nreturn output; // JSON"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1773642068029"
          },
          "code": "GROUP_BY_ITEMNUMBER",
          "id": "1773640874702",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Get Top 3 Items",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const grouped = $context.$nodes.GROUP_BY_ITEMNUMBER.$output?.result;\nconst items = grouped?.items ?? [];\n\nconst toNum = (v) => {\n  const n = Number(v);\n  return Number.isFinite(n) ? n : 0;\n};\n\nconst threshold = toNum($context.$variables.threshold);\n\n// Shortage definition\nconst isShortage = (ps) =>\n  toNum(ps.PctDiffTotal) > threshold || toNum(ps.PctDiffFull) > threshold;\n\nconst scored = items.map((it) => {\n  const pullSequences = it.pullSequences ?? [];\n  const shortagePullSequences = pullSequences.filter(isShortage);\n\n  const pullSequenceCount = pullSequences.length;\n  const shortageCount = shortagePullSequences.length;\n\n  const maxPctDiff = pullSequences.reduce((maxSoFar, ps) => {\n    const severity = Math.max(toNum(ps.PctDiffFull), toNum(ps.PctDiffTotal));\n    return Math.max(maxSoFar, severity);\n  }, 0);\n\n  const maxShortagePctDiff = shortagePullSequences.reduce((maxSoFar, ps) => {\n    const severity = Math.max(toNum(ps.PctDiffFull), toNum(ps.PctDiffTotal));\n    return Math.max(maxSoFar, severity);\n  }, 0);\n\n  const Badge =\n    shortageCount === 0\n      ? \"No Shortage\"\n      : pullSequenceCount === shortageCount\n        ? \"Shortage\"\n        : \"Partial Shortage\";\n\n  return {\n    itemNumber: it.itemNumber ?? null,\n    organizationId: it.organizationId ?? grouped?.organizationId ?? null,\n    inventoryItemId: it.inventoryItemId ?? null,\n    itemDescription: it.itemDescription ?? null,\n\n    pullSequenceCount,\n    shortageCount,\n    Badge,\n\n    maxPctDiff,\n    maxShortagePctDiff,\n\n    pullSequencesDetails: pullSequences\n  };\n});\n\nconst withShortages = scored.filter((x) => x.shortageCount > 0);\n\nwithShortages.sort((a, b) => {\n  // 1) Higher shortageCount first\n  const byShortageCount = b.shortageCount - a.shortageCount;\n  if (byShortageCount) return byShortageCount;\n\n  // 2) If same shortageCount, prioritize full-shortage items\n  const aIsFullShortage = a.shortageCount === a.pullSequenceCount ? 1 : 0;\n  const bIsFullShortage = b.shortageCount === b.pullSequenceCount ? 1 : 0;\n  const byFullShortage = bIsFullShortage - aIsFullShortage;\n  if (byFullShortage) return byFullShortage;\n\n  // 3) Then greater (pullSequenceCount - shortageCount) first\n  const aGap = a.pullSequenceCount - a.shortageCount;\n  const bGap = b.pullSequenceCount - b.shortageCount;\n  const byGap = bGap - aGap;\n  if (byGap) return byGap;\n\n  // Stable final tie-breaker\n  return String(a.itemNumber).localeCompare(String(b.itemNumber));\n});\n\nconst top3 = withShortages.slice(0, 3);\n\nreturn {\n  organizationId: grouped?.organizationId ?? null,\n  criteria: {\n    shortageDefinition: `PctDiffTotal > ${threshold} OR PctDiffFull > ${threshold}`,\n    sortOrder: [\n      \"shortageCount desc\",\n      \"isFullShortage desc (shortageCount == pullSequenceCount)\",\n      \"(pullSequenceCount - shortageCount) desc\"\n    ],\n    topN: 3\n  },\n  totalItemsEvaluated: scored.length,\n  itemsWithShortage: withShortages.length,\n  topItems: top3\n};"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1773640347522"
          },
          "code": "GET_TOP_3_ITEMS",
          "id": "1773642068029",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Summarizer"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "SUMMARIZER",
          "id": "1773644441060",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1773644441061_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a user-facing summarization agent operating inside Oracle Fusion Cloud.\n\nYou will receive a JSON array representing item-wise Kanban health results. {{$context.$nodes. GET_TOP_3_ITEMS.$output.result}} - \n\nYour task is to summarize the input into 3–4 short, clear lines suitable for display in a message widget. Never tell anything about overstocking, only understocked and items which are just about to be understocked, that is, just near the lower threshold.\n\nInstructions:\n- Summarize the overall Kanban health across items. Do not use words like \"Mixed\", just state facts.\n- Highlight which items require attention, if any.\n- Briefly indicate the extent of the issue (for example: how many pull sequences are affected).\n\nRules:\n- Limit the output to a maximum of 2 lines.\n- Do NOT mention JSON, field names, thresholds, or calculations.\n- Do NOT include technical or developer terminology.\n- Use plain, business-friendly English.\n- Be concise and easy to scan.\n- Output plain text only (no JSON, no bullets)."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": false
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Init Actions Agent"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "INIT_ACTIONS_AGENT",
          "id": "1773645212564",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1773645212566_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an action-recommendation agent operating inside Oracle Fusion Cloud.\n\nINPUT\n- top3Items: {{$context.$nodes.GET_TOP_3_ITEMS.$output.result}}\n- threshold: {{$context.$variables.threshold}}\n\nTASK\nGenerate priority actions for eligible items in the Top 3 list.\n\nDATA KEYS (STRICT / EXACT)\n1. Read items only from: top3Items.topItems\n2. Item identifier key: item.itemNumber\n3. Pull sequence array key: item.pullSequencesDetails\n4. Pull sequence identifier key: seq.pullSequenceId\n5. Percentage keys (from pull sequence only): seq.PctDiffTotal, seq.PctDiffFull\n6. Do not read percentage values from item root.\n\nNUMERIC CONVERSION (STRICT / MANDATORY)\nFor each pull sequence seq:\n1. pctDiffTotalNum = parseFloat(seq.PctDiffTotal)\n2. pctDiffFullNum = parseFloat(seq.PctDiffFull)\n3. If parseFloat returns NaN, set that value to 0.\n4. Preserve sign exactly (e.g., \"-10\" remains -10).\n\nISSUE RULE (STRICT)\nUse precomputed eligibility only:\n1. An item is eligible if item.shortageCount > 0\n2. Do not recompute eligibility from seq.PctDiffTotal or seq.PctDiffFull\n\nGENERATION RULES (STRICT)\n1. Iterate every item in top3Items.topItems.\n2. For each item, inspect all item.pullSequencesDetails.\n3. If at least one pull sequence is an issue, generate exactly ONE action for that item.\n4. Use the first pull sequence in item.pullSequencesDetails where parseFloat(PctDiffTotal) > threshold OR parseFloat(PctDiffFull) > threshold for followUpCommand.\n5. Never generate more than one action per item.itemNumber.\n6. Do not skip eligible items.\n7. Maximum actions = number of eligible items in top3Items (up to 3).\n8. If no eligible items exist, return an empty actions array.\n\nSHORT DESCRIPTION RULE (STRICT)\nFor the chosen issue pull sequence:\n1. If pctDiffTotalNum > threshold:\n   Total kanban cards are below the threshold.\n2. Else:\n   Kanban cards in Full status are below the threshold.\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT (STRICT / JSON ONLY)\nReturn each action as a JSON object in this exact shape:\n\n    {\n      \"title\": \"<item.itemNumber>\",\n      \"shortDescription\": \"<resolved shortDescription>\",\n      \"actionText\": \"Generate and replenish temporary kanban cards\",\n      \"followUpCommand\": \"ora.Invoke(\\\"generateTemporaryKanbanCard\\\", \\\"generateTemporaryKanbanCard-<seq.pullSequenceId>\\\")\",\n      \"priority\": true\n    }\n\nOUTPUT CONSTRAINTS (HARD)\n1. Output valid JSON only.\n2. No markdown, no prose, no explanations, no comments.\n3. No extra keys.\n4. No placeholder tokens in final output values.\n5. Do not output internal reasoning or raw analysis.\n6. Excess stock and normal ranges are healthy; never create actions for them.\n\nFINAL VALIDATION (MANDATORY)\n1.1. Compute eligibleItemCount = number of items where item.shortageCount > 0.\n2. Output count must satisfy: `actions.length === eligibleItemCount`.\n3. If `eligibleItemCount === 0`, output nothing."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Get Pull Sequence Id",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const suggestedAction = $context.$triggers.REST.$input.OraAction;\nconst [action, pullSequenceId] = suggestedAction .split(\"-\", 2);\n\nreturn {Action: action, PullSequenceId: pullSequenceId};"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1775726826445"
          },
          "code": "GET_PULL_SEQUENCE_ID",
          "id": "1773645922160",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Run Actions"
          },
          "outcomes": {
