          },
          "code": "CONTEXT_SWITCH",
          "convergenceTargetId": "end",
          "id": "1774247776940",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1774247776941_1",
              "name": "caseExpression",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.CONTEXT_INDENTIFYING_AGENT.$output.context}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "SWITCH"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MESSAGES_LIST",
                "ORA_LAYOUT_CARD"
              ],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": false,
              "customNotes": "You are a user-facing message widget agent operating inside Oracle Fusion Cloud.\n\n\nRENDERING RULES (MUST FOLLOW)\n- Heading (inside the widget): \"Kanban Items Needing Attention\".\n- Render one messageList row/card per array element.\n- For each row/card:\n  - title = Title\n  - Subtitle = CardDetails\n  - Body = PullSequenceDetails\n  - Body = MoreInfo\n  - Body = Add exactly **one** action with the followUpCommand:\n    {\n      \"followUpCommand\": \"ora.Invoke(NavigateToKanbanItemDetailsApp, {\\\"organizationId\\\":{{$context.$variables.organizationId}},\\\"organizationCode\\\":\\\"{{$context.$variables.organizationCode}}\\\",\\\"organizationName\\\":\\\"{{$context.$variables.organizationName}}\\\",\\\"threshold\\\":\\\"{{$context.$variables.threshold}}\\\",\\\"inventoryItemId\\\":<inventoryItemId>})\",\n      \"shortDescription\": \"Navigate to Kanban Item Details App\"\n    }\n- Badge\n\nFor BADGES :\n- Each item MUST have exactly ONE badge, represented only by the field Badge in {{$context.$nodes.GET_SHORTAGE_PULL_SEQUENCES_FOR_POU.$output.result}}\nNo variations allowed. \n\nTONE for Badge\n- Direct and operational\n- Neutral if stable\n- Caution if Partial Shortage\n- Strong and urgent if Shortage\n- Shortage and Partial Shortage will be decided only and only based on the Badge field in the input corresponding to each item: {{$context.$nodes.GET_SHORTAGE_PULL_SEQUENCES_FOR_POU.$output.result}}\n\n- Do NOT display any IDs in visible text.\n- Ensure followUpCommand is a single quoted string and the JSON is syntactically valid (escape inner quotes as needed).\n- Output ONLY the messageListWidget JSON (no additional text, no markdown).\n- DO NOT wrap in quotes\n- DO NOT escape quotes\n- DO NOT change order of fields\n- Keep everything else EXACTLY as shown\n- No extra spaces or formatting changes"
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "POU Query Agent"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "POU_QUERY_AGENT",
          "id": "1774248104185",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1774248104186_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a user-facing explanation agent inside Oracle Fusion Cloud.\n\n────────────────────────────────────────\nINPUTS\n- pullSequenceSummaries: {{$context.$nodes.GET_SHORTAGE_PULL_SEQUENCES_FOR_POU.$output.result}};\n- contextType: {{$context.$nodes.CONTEXT_INDENTIFYING_AGENT.$output}}\n- userQuery: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n- chatHistory: {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\n- threshold: {{$context.$variables.threshold}}\n\n────────────────────────────────────────\nAUTHORITATIVE BUSINESS RULES (MUST FOLLOW)\n- Only shortages require attention.\n- A pull sequence needs attention if (inclusive OR):\n  - parseFloat(PctDiffTotal) > threshold, OR\n  - parseFloat(PctDiffFull) > threshold\n- Guardrail: This is an OR condition. Do NOT treat it as AND.\n- PctDiffTotal and PctDiffFull may be strings:\n  - Always convert to numbers using parseFloat before comparing.\n  - If null/empty/missing/non-numeric, treat as 0.\n- Excess stock and normal ranges are healthy and must NOT be treated as issues.\n- Do not invent or assume missing data.\n\n────────────────────────────────────────\nEMPTY DATA HANDLING (MUST FOLLOW)\n- If pullSequenceSummaries is is null/empty:\n  Output exactly one plain-English line and nothing else:\n  \"There are no shortages for any item in the current organization.\"\n\n────────────────────────────────────────\nINTERNAL ANALYSIS (DO NOT DISPLAY)\n- For each ItemNumber, fetch the following from groupedItemMetrics by matching itemNumber:\n   - FullCards\n   - EmptyCard\n   - NewCards\n   - InprocessCards\n   - TemporaryCards\n   - shortagePullSequences\n   - totalPullSequences\n   - badge\n- Never show IDs or internal field names in the final response.\n- Do not include intermediate calculations, formulas, or thresholds in the final response.\n\n────────────────────────────────────────\nOUTPUT FORMAT\n[\n{\n    Title: <ItemNumber>,\n    CardDetails: “<Full> FULL | <Empty> EMPTY | <New> NEW | <InProcess> IN PROCESS | <temporary> TEMPORARY”,\n    PullSequenceDetails: “<shortagePullSequences>/<totalPullSequences> pull sequences need attention”\n    Actiona: action to navigate to item details app.\n },....\n]\n\n- Replace the <Full>, <Empty>, <New>, <Inprocess>,  <temporary>, <shortagePullSequences>, <totalPullSequences> from the internal analysis made.\n\n────────────────────────────────────────\n\nACTION (MUST FOLLOW)\n- Add exactly one action per row:\n  - followUpCommand must navigate to item details:\n    ora.Invoke(NavigateToKanbanItemDetailsApp, {\"organizationId\":{{$context.$variables.organizationId}},\"organizationCode\":\"{{$context.$variables.organizationCode}}\",\"organizationName\":\"{{$context.$variables.organizationName}}\",\"inventoryItemId\":<inventoryItemId>})\n- Replacement rules:\n  - Replace <inventoryItemId> with the InventoryItemId for that ItemNumber (choose the InventoryItemId from any pull sequence in the group; they will be the same per item).\n  - Do NOT display inventoryItemId (or any IDs) in visible text; only include it inside followUpCommand.\n- Ensure the entire followUpCommand value (including closing parentheses) is inside quotes.\n- DO NOT wrap in quotes\n- DO NOT escape quotes\n- DO NOT change order of fields\n- Keep everything else EXACTLY as shown\n- No extra spaces or formatting changes\n\n────────────────────────────────────────\n\nRESPONSE REQUIREMENTS (MUST FOLLOW)\n- Produce a concise, business-friendly summary of shortages only.\n- Do not flag excess stock or normal ranges as problems.\n- Do not include internal labels, IDs, raw JSON fields, or hidden reasoning.\n- Use clear line breaks for readability."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MESSAGES_LIST",
                "ORA_LAYOUT_CARD"
              ],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": false
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Query Agent"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "QUERY_AGENT",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1774248214905",
          "id": "1773660978990",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1773660978992_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a user-facing explanation agent inside Oracle Fusion Cloud.\n\nINPUTS\n- pullSequenceSummaries: {{$context.$nodes.GET_PULLSEQUENCE_SUMMARIES_FOR_QUERY.$output}}\n- contextType: {{$context.$nodes.CONTEXT_INDENTIFYING_AGENT.$output}}\n- userQuery: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n- chatHistory: {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT\n[\n{\n    Title: <ItemNumber>,\n    CardDetails: “<Full> FULL | <Empty> EMPTY | <New> NEW | <InProcess> IN PROCESS”,\n    PullSequenceDetails: “<shortagePullSequences>/<totalPullSequences> pull sequences need attention”\n    MoreInfo: “For more information click on:”,\n    ActionableButton: action button to navigate to item details app.\n}\n]\n- Replace the <Full>, <Empty>, <New>, <Inprocess>, <shortagePullSequences>, <totalPullSequences> from the internal analysis made.\n────────────────────────────────────────\nACTION (MUST FOLLOW)\n- ONE ACTION for the given single Item Number:\n  - followUpCommand must navigate to item details:\n    ora.Invoke(NavigateToKanbanItemDetailsApp,{\\\"organizationId\\\":{{$context.$variables.organizationId}},\\\"organizationCode\\\":\\\"{{$context.$variables.organizationCode}}\\\",\\\"organizationName\\\":\\\"{{$context.$variables.organizationName}}\\\",\\\"threshold\\\":\\\"{{$context.$variables.threshold}}\\\",\\\"inventoryItemId\\\":<inventoryItemId>}) \n- Replacement rules:\n  - Replace <inventoryItemId> with the InventoryItemId for that ItemNumber (choose the InventoryItemId from any pull sequence in the group; they will be the same per item).\n  - Do NOT display inventoryItemId (or any IDs) in visible text; only include it inside followUpCommand.\n- Ensure the entire followUpCommand value (including closing parentheses) is inside quotes.\n- DO NOT wrap in quotes\n- DO NOT escape quotes\n- DO NOT change order of fields\n- Keep everything else EXACTLY as shown\n- No extra spaces or formatting changes\n────────────────────────────────────────\nRESPONSE REQUIREMENTS (MUST FOLLOW)\n- Produce a concise, business-friendly summary of shortages only.\n- Do not flag excess stock or normal ranges as problems.\n- Do not include internal labels, IDs, raw JSON fields, or hidden reasoning.\n- Use clear line breaks for readability.\n\n- FOR EVERY ROW GENERATED FOR AN ITEM, IT MUST HAVE AN ACTION ASSOCIATED WITH IT. \n\nAUTHORITATIVE BUSINESS RULES (MUST FOLLOW)\n1. Respond directly and accurately to the userQuery using pullSequenceSummaries and contextType.\n2. Keep the response concise, clear, and user-facing.\n3. If no data relevant to the userQuery is found, respond with exactly:\n   Please specify a context like an item or a point of use.\n"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MESSAGES_LIST",
                "ORA_LAYOUT_CARD"
              ],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": false,
              "customNotes": "You are a user-facing message widget agent operating inside Oracle Fusion Cloud.\n\nRENDERING RULES (MUST FOLLOW)\n- Heading (inside widget): \"Kanban Items Needing Attention\".\n- Render one messageList row/card per item in itemCards.\n- For each card:\n  - title = Title\n  - subtitle = CardDetails\n  - body = PullSequenceDetails\n  - Body = Add exactly **one** action as the followUpCommand:\n    {\n      \"followUpCommand\": ora.Invoke(NavigateToKanbanItemDetailsApp, {\"organizationId\":{{$context.$variables.organizationId}},\"organizationCode\":\"{{$context.$variables.organizationCode}}\",\"organizationName\":\"{{$context.$variables.organizationName}}\",\"threshold\":\"{{$context.$variables.threshold}}\",\"inventoryItemId\":<inventoryItemId>}),\n      \"shortDescription\": \"Navigate to Kanban Item Details App\"\n    }\n- Badge\n\nFor BADGES :\n- Each item MUST have exactly ONE badge, represented only by the field Badge in {{$context.$nodes.GET_SHORTAGE_PULL_SEQUENCES.$output.result}}\nNo variations allowed. \n\nTONE for Badge\n- Direct and operational\n- Neutral if stable\n- Caution if Partial Shortage\n- Strong and urgent if Shortage\n- Shortage and Partial Shortage will be decided only and only based on the Badge field in the input corresponding to each item: {{$context.$nodes.GET_SHORTAGE_PULL_SEQUENCES.$output.result}}\n\nDATA + SAFETY RULES (MUST FOLLOW)\n- Do not display any IDs in visible text.\n- Every rendered row must include exactly one action.\n- If itemCards is null/empty, return a valid messageListWidget JSON with heading and zero rows.\n- Output ONLY the messageListWidget JSON.\n- No markdown.\n- No explanatory text outside JSON.\n- Do not change order of fields in each row/action object."
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Item Query Agent"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "ITEM_QUERY_AGENT",
          "id": "1774251872095",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1774251872096_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a user-facing explanation agent inside Oracle Fusion Cloud.\n\nINPUTS\n- groupedItemMetrics: {{$context.$nodes.GET_SHORTAGE_PULL_SEQUENCES.$output.result}}\n- contextType: {{$context.$nodes.CONTEXT_INDENTIFYING_AGENT.$output}}\n- userQuery: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n- chatHistory: {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\n- threshold: {{$context.$variables.threshold}}\n\nBUSINESS RULES (AUTHORITATIVE)\n1. Only shortages require attention.\n2. A pull sequence needs attention if:\n   - parseFloat(PctDiffTotal) > threshold OR parseFloat(PctDiffFull) > threshold\n3. This is OR logic only (never AND).\n4. PctDiffTotal/PctDiffFull may be strings; always convert to numeric.\n5. Null/empty/missing/non-numeric numeric fields must be treated as 0.\n6. Excess stock and normal ranges are healthy and must not be flagged.\n\nEMPTY DATA RULE (STRICT)\nIf groupedItemMetrics is null/empty, output exactly:\nThere are no shortages for this item in the current organization.\nOutput nothing else.\n\nINTERNAL COMPUTATION (DO NOT SHOW)\n1. For each ItemNumber, fetch the following from groupedItemMetrics by matching itemNumber:\n   - FullCards\n   - EmptyCards\n   - NewCards\n   - InprocessCards\n   - TemporaryCards\n   - shortagePullSequences\n   - totalPullSequences\n   - badge\n2. If badge is missing in groupedItemMetrics, derive it as:\n   - badge = \"Shortage\" when shortagePullSequences == totalPullSequences\n   - badge = \"Partial Shortage\" when shortagePullSequences < totalPullSequences\n3. For each ItemNumber, get inventoryItemId from any row in that item group.\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT (STRICT ORDER)\n\n-For each Item Number:\n{\nTitle: <ItemNumber>,\nCardDetails: \"<Full> FULL | <Empty> EMPTY | <New> NEW | <InProcess> IN PROCESS | <temporary> TEMPORARY\",\nPullSequenceDetails: \"<shortagePullSequences>/<totalPullSequences> pull sequences need attention\",\nAction: {followUpCommand: ora.Invoke(NavigateToKanbanItemDetailsApp,{\"organizationId\":{{$context.$variables.organizationId}},\"organizationCode\":\"{{$context.$variables.organizationCode}}\",\"organizationName\":\"{{$context.$variables.organizationName}}\",\"threshold\":\"{{$context.$variables.threshold}}\",\"inventoryItemId\":<inventoryItemId>})}\nBadge: <badge>\n}\n\n\n\nACTION RULES (STRICT)\n1. Generate one action per ItemNumber.\n2. Every row must have its own followUpCommand.\n3. Replace <inventoryItemId> with that item’s computed InventoryItemId.\n4. Do not display inventoryItemId or any internal IDs in visible text.\n5. Keep followUpCommand exactly in the format above (no escaping, no reordering).\n\nRESPONSE STYLE\n1. Concise, business-friendly, shortage-focused.\n2. Mention that users can click the item to view more details.\n3. Do not expose raw fields, hidden reasoning, or internal labels.\n4. Do not add last updated by or extra fields."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "errorNodeId": "1773737397895",
            "name": "Get Shortage Pull Sequences",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const input = $context.$nodes.GET_PULLSEQUENCE_SUMMARIES_FOR_QUERY?.$output;\nconst items = Array.isArray(input?.items) ? input.items : [];\n\nconst toNum = (v) => {\n  if (v === null || v === undefined) return 0;\n  const n = parseFloat(String(v).replace(/,/g, \"\").replace(\"%\", \"\").trim());\n  return Number.isFinite(n) ? n : 0;\n};\n\nconst threshold = toNum($context.$variables.threshold);\n\nconst grouped = items.reduce((acc, r) => {\n  const itemNumber = r?.ItemNumber ?? null;\n  const key = itemNumber === null ? \"__NULL__\" : String(itemNumber);\n\n  if (!acc[key]) {\n    acc[key] = {\n      itemNumber,\n      items: []\n    };\n  }\n\n  acc[key].items.push(r);\n  return acc;\n}, {});\n\nconst x = Object.values(grouped)\n  .map((g) => {\n    const totalPullSequences = new Set(\n      g.items\n        .map((r) => r?.PullSequenceId)\n        .filter((id) => id !== null && id !== undefined && String(id).trim() !== \"\")\n    ).size;\n\n    let shortagePullSequences = 0;\n\n    let FullCards = 0;\n    let NewCards = 0;\n    let EmptyCards = 0;\n    let InprocessCards = 0;\n    let TemporaryCards = 0;\n\n    for (const r of g.items) {\n      const pctDiffTotalNum = toNum(r?.PctDiffTotal);\n      const pctDiffFullNum = toNum(r?.PctDiffFull);\n\n      if (pctDiffTotalNum > threshold || pctDiffFullNum > threshold) {\n        shortagePullSequences += 1;\n      }\n\n      FullCards += toNum(r?.FullCards);\n      NewCards += toNum(r?.NewCards);\n      EmptyCards += toNum(r?.EmptyCards);\n      InprocessCards += toNum(r?.InprocessCards);\n      TemporaryCards += toNum(r?.TemporaryCards);\n    }\n\n    const badge =\n      totalPullSequences > 0 && shortagePullSequences === totalPullSequences\n        ? \"Shortage\"\n        : \"Partial Shortage\";\nconst inventoryItemId =\n  g.items.find(r => r?.InventoryItemId != null)?.InventoryItemId ?? null;\n    return {\n      ...g,\n      shortagePullSequences,\n      totalPullSequences,\n      inventoryItemId,\n      Badge: badge,\n      FullCards,\n      NewCards,\n      EmptyCards,\n      InprocessCards,\n      TemporaryCards\n    };\n  })\n  .filter((g) => g.shortagePullSequences > 0);\n\nreturn x;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1774251872095"
          },
          "code": "GET_SHORTAGE_PULL_SEQUENCES",
          "id": "1774255972867",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Get Shortage Pull Sequences for POU",
            "returnType": "array",
            "sourceCode": "const input = $context.$nodes.GET_PULLSEQUENCE_SUMMARIES_FOR_QUERY?.$output;\nconst items = Array.isArray(input?.items) ? input.items : [];\n\nconst toNum = (v) => {\n  if (v === null || v === undefined) return 0;\n  const n = parseFloat(String(v).replace(/,/g, \"\").replace(\"%\", \"\").trim());\n  return Number.isFinite(n) ? n : 0;\n};\n\n\nconst threshold = toNum($context.$variables.threshold);\n\nconst grouped = items.reduce((acc, r) => {\n  const itemNumber = r?.ItemNumber ?? null;\n  const key = itemNumber === null ? \"__NULL__\" : String(itemNumber);\n\n  if (!acc[key]) {\n    acc[key] = {\n      itemNumber,\n      items: []\n    };\n  }\n\n  acc[key].items.push(r);\n  return acc;\n}, {});\n\nconst x = Object.values(grouped).map((g) => {\n  const totalPullSequences = new Set(\n    g.items\n      .map((r) => r?.PullSequenceId)\n      .filter((id) => id !== null && id !== undefined && String(id).trim() !== \"\")\n  ).size;\n\n  let shortagePullSequences = 0;\n\n  let FullCards = 0;\n  let NewCards = 0;\n  let EmptyCards = 0;\n  let InprocessCards = 0;\n  let TemporaryCards = 0;\n\n  for (const r of g.items) {\n    const pctDiffTotalNum = toNum(r?.PctDiffTotal);\n    const pctDiffFullNum = toNum(r?.PctDiffFull);\n\n    if (pctDiffTotalNum > threshold || pctDiffFullNum > threshold) {\n      shortagePullSequences += 1;\n    }\n\n    FullCards += toNum(r?.FullCards);\n    NewCards += toNum(r?.NewCards);\n    EmptyCards += toNum(r?.EmptyCards);\n    InprocessCards += toNum(r?.InprocessCards);\n    TemporaryCards += toNum(r?.TemporaryCards);\n  }\n\n  const badge =\n    totalPullSequences > 0 && shortagePullSequences === totalPullSequences\n      ? \"Shortage\"\n      : \"Partial Shortage\";\nconst inventoryItemId =\n  g.items.find(r => r?.InventoryItemId != null)?.InventoryItemId ?? null;\n  return {\n    ...g,\n    shortagePullSequences,\n    totalPullSequences,\n    Badge: badge,\ninventoryItemId,\n    FullCards,\n    NewCards,\n    EmptyCards,\n    InprocessCards,\n    TemporaryCards\n  };\n});\n\nreturn x;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1774248104185"
          },
          "code": "GET_SHORTAGE_PULL_SEQUENCES_FOR_POU",
          "id": "1774257714884",
